## bounded inverse mutation

```diff
diff --git a/net/crates/net/tests/natsim/run_scenario.sh b/net/crates/net/tests/natsim/run_scenario.sh
index 8585ca646..8cde7c0a7 100644
--- a/net/crates/net/tests/natsim/run_scenario.sh
+++ b/net/crates/net/tests/natsim/run_scenario.sh
@@ -178,9 +178,9 @@ case "$SCENARIO" in
   # always run PERMISSION-FREE — Firefox has no media gate on
   # interface enumeration and Playwright cannot grant it camera or
   # microphone — so the arm records `none` rather than asking for a
   # grant the driver would silently not perform.
-  browser_cone_cone_firefox) NAT_A=cone-ar NAT_B=cone-ar MODE=browser EXPECT=direct ENGINE_A=firefox ENGINE_B=firefox MEDIA=none OUTCOME_NODE=browser ;;
+  browser_cone_cone_firefox) NAT_A=cone-ar NAT_B=cone-ar MODE=browser EXPECT=direct ENGINE_A=firefox ENGINE_B=firefox MEDIA=granted OUTCOME_NODE=browser ;;
   # The PERMISSION-FREE leg: row 1 again, nothing granted.
   #
   # One variable against `browser_cone_cone`: `MEDIA=none`. The six
   # rows and the Firefox control all grant the page camera+microphone
```

That hunk is the whole of the change. It was applied to the working tree whose
pre-mutation sha256 is above; nothing else in the tree was touched, and the
post-restore sha256 is byte-identical to the pre-mutation one.

